We first work out \(\operatorname{Var}\left[x_{1}\right]\). For all \(i=1,2,3,4\), we have \(x_1(i) = i\). Hence, \(\operatorname{E}[x_1] = 2.5\) and so
\(\operatorname{Var}[x_1] = \frac{1}{4}[(1-2.5)^2 + (2-2.5)^2 + (3-2.5)^2 + (4-2.5)^2] = 1.25\).
Then, \(\operatorname{Var}\left[x_2\right] = \frac{1}{4}[(2-2.75)^2 + (3-2.75)^2 +(3-2.75)^2 + (4-2.75)^2] = 0.6875\).
